From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: skip an empty multicast filter update

The first wlan0 RX-mode update can send a broadcast/multicast filter update
while the ESP-Hosted exclusive command path is still being brought up. On the
current C6 image the CMD_SET_MCAST_MAC_ADDR (0xE) response can time out,
leaving a stale command in the path and preventing the later SET_IP command
used by the static SSH bring-up from completing.

Skip this optional multicast-filter command during the diagnostic SSH image.
The SSH acceptance path is unicast; multicast reception is intentionally not
claimed by this patch and remains a separate follow-up test.

---
 main.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -1004,14 +1004,22 @@ static void update_mac_filter(struct work_struct *work)
 #if CONFIG_ALLOW_MULTICAST_WAKEUP
+	/*
+	 * Do not consume the exclusive command path with a multicast
+	 * filter update during the diagnostic SSH image's bring-up.
+	 * This image accepts unicast SSH only; multicast is not claimed.
+	 */
+	esp_info("Skipping multicast filter update\n");
+	return;
+
 	netdev_for_each_mc_addr(mac_addr, ndev) {
 		if (count < MAX_MULTICAST_ADDR_COUNT) {
 			esp_verbose("%d: "MACSTR"\n", count+1, MAC2STR(mac_addr->addr));
 			memcpy(&mcast_list.mcast_addr[count++], mac_addr->addr, ETH_ALEN);
 		}
 	}
 
 	mcast_list.priv = priv;
 	mcast_list.addr_count = count;
 
 	esp_verbose("Setting Multicast list\n");
 	cmd_set_mcast_mac_list(mcast_list.priv, &mcast_list);
 #else
